          "pubDate": "Tue, 05 Nov 2024 13:33:39 +0000",
          "title": "Dragon Approaching Station on 31st Cargo Mission",
        },
        {
          "category": [
            "Commercial Resupply Services",
            "International Space Station",
            "Kennedy Space Center",
            "NASA",
            "Launch Complex 39A",
            "NASA's SpaceX 31st Resupply Mission",
          ],
          "content:encoded": "<figure id="attachment_25580" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-25580" style="width: 840px" class="wp-caption alignleft"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-25580" src="https://blogs.nasa.gov/commercialresupply/wp-content/uploads/sites/381/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png" alt="" width="840" height="455" srcset="https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png 2694w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=300,163 300w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=768,416 768w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=1024,555 1024w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=1536,832 1536w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=2048,1110 2048w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/CRS-31-Launch.png?resize=1200,650 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 709px) 85vw, (max-width: 909px) 67vw, (max-width: 1362px) 62vw, 840px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-25580" class="wp-caption-text">The SpaceX Dragon spacecraft, carrying more than 6,000 pounds of supplies to the orbiting laboratory, lifted off at 9:29 p.m. EST Monday, on the company’s Falcon 9 rocket from Launch Complex 39A at NASA’s Kennedy Space Center in Florida. Credits: NASA+</figcaption></figure>
<p>At 9:29 p.m. EST, over 6,000 pounds of scientific investigations and cargo launched to the International Space Station on the SpaceX Dragon spacecraft for the company’s 31st commercial resupply services mission for NASA. The spacecraft lifted off on a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket from Launch Complex 39A at NASA&#8217;s Kennedy Space Center in Florida.</p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">About 9 minutes after launch, Dragon will separate from the rocket’s second stage, open its nosecone, and begin a carefully choreographed series of thruster firings to reach the space station.</span> <span data-ccp-props="{&quot;134233279&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">Dragon will arrive at the orbiting outpost at 10:15 a.m. Tuesday, Nov. 5, and dock autonomously to the forward port of the space station’s Harmony module.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot;134233279&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">NASA will provide live coverage of the spacecraft’s arrival beginning at 8:45 a.m. Nov. 5 on </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/scheduled-video/nasas-spacex-31st-cargo-resupply-services-rendezvous-and-docking/"><span data-contrast="none">NASA+</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and the agency’s </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/"><span data-contrast="none">website</span></a><span data-contrast="none">.</span><span data-contrast="none"> Learn how to </span><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/general/how-to-stream-nasa-tv/"><span data-contrast="none">watch NASA content</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> through a variety of platforms, including social </span><span data-contrast="none">media.</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">Learn more about station activities by following the </span><a href="https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/"><span data-contrast="none">space station blog</span></a><span data-contrast="none">, </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.twitter.com%2Fspace_station&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=IV%2Fk%2BtrgJqB%2FY3vfFBms%2FzYyFo7NjSY7ZtrCnj8oCvc%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">@space_station</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.twitter.com%2FISS_Research&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=%2BTImkF1bp%2FnuNx0nf1Yt2v7brAheJ%2FKuZqdLGOJdEME%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">@ISS_Research</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> on X as well as the </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fiss&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=kd6yViXDt22Nh0QquqXdd7F6%2FzC6ygUOPn2hrClv6FQ%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">ISS Facebook</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fiss&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=tORQzcWS9eXQrG0Y0nXeXlTWgq6nxoPDODMNaHH29aI%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">ISS Instagram</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> accounts.</span></p>
",
          "dc:creator": "Stephanie Plucinsky",
          "description": "At 9:29 p.m. EST, over 6,000 pounds of scientific investigations and cargo launched to the International Space Station on the SpaceX Dragon spacecraft for the company’s 31st commercial resupply services mission for NASA. The spacecraft lifted off on a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket from Launch Complex 39A at NASA&#8217;s Kennedy Space Center in Florida. About &#8230; ",
          "guid": "https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/2024/11/04/nasas-spacex-crs-31-dragon-launches-at-929-p-m-est/",
          "link": "https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/2024/11/04/nasas-spacex-crs-31-dragon-launches-at-929-p-m-est/",
          "pubDate": "Tue, 05 Nov 2024 02:39:22 +0000",
          "title": "NASA’s SpaceX CRS-31: Dragon Launches at 9:29 p.m. EST",
        },
        {
          "category": [
            "International Space Station",
            "Kennedy Space Center",
            "Launch Complex 39A",
            "NASA's SpaceX 31st Resupply Mission",
          ],
          "content:encoded": "<figure id="attachment_25573" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-25573" style="width: 840px" class="wp-caption alignleft"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-25573" src="https://blogs.nasa.gov/commercialresupply/wp-content/uploads/sites/381/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg" alt="" width="840" height="560" srcset="https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg 1280w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg?resize=300,200 300w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg?resize=768,512 768w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg?resize=1024,682 1024w, https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/wp-content/uploads/sites/240/2024/11/KSC-20241103-PH-SPX01_0001medium.jpg?resize=1200,800 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 709px) 85vw, (max-width: 909px) 67vw, (max-width: 1362px) 62vw, 840px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-25573" class="wp-caption-text">A SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket, with the company’s Dragon spacecraft atop, stands in a vertical position at Launch Complex 39A at NASA’s Kennedy Space Center in Florida on Monday, Nov. 4, 2024, in preparation for the 31st commercial resupply services launch to the International Space Station. Photo credit: NASA+</figcaption></figure>
<p><span data-contrast="none">NASA’s coverage is underway on </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/scheduled-video/nasas-spacex-31st-cargo-resupply-services-launch/"><span data-contrast="none">NASA+</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and the agency’s </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/"><span data-contrast="none">website</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> for the launch of SpaceX’s 31st commercial resupply services mission to the International Space Station. </span><span data-contrast="none">Learn how to </span><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/general/how-to-stream-nasa-tv/"><span data-contrast="none">watch NASA content</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> through a variety of platforms, including social </span><span data-contrast="none">media.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot;134233279&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">The SpaceX Dragon spacecraft is scheduled for liftoff at 9:29 p.m. EST on the company’s Falcon 9 rocket from Launch Complex 39A at NASA’s Kennedy Space Center in Florida.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot;134233279&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}"> </span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">Filled with more than 6,000 pounds of scientific investigations, food, supplies, and equipment, Dragon will arrive at the orbiting outpost at 10:15 a.m. Tuesday, Nov. 5, and dock autonomously to the forward port of the space station’s Harmony module.</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">NASA will provide live coverage of the spacecraft’s arrival beginning at 8:45 a.m. Nov. 5 on </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/scheduled-video/nasas-spacex-31st-cargo-resupply-services-rendezvous-and-docking/"><span data-contrast="none">NASA+</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and the agency’s </span><a href="https://plus.nasa.gov/"><span data-contrast="none">website</span></a><span data-contrast="none">.</span></p>
<p><span data-contrast="none">Learn more about station activities by following the </span><a href="https://blogs.nasa.gov/spacestation/"><span data-contrast="none">space station blog</span></a><span data-contrast="none">, </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.twitter.com%2Fspace_station&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=IV%2Fk%2BtrgJqB%2FY3vfFBms%2FzYyFo7NjSY7ZtrCnj8oCvc%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">@space_station</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.twitter.com%2FISS_Research&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=%2BTImkF1bp%2FnuNx0nf1Yt2v7brAheJ%2FKuZqdLGOJdEME%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">@ISS_Research</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> on X as well as the </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fiss&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=kd6yViXDt22Nh0QquqXdd7F6%2FzC6ygUOPn2hrClv6FQ%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">ISS Facebook</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> and </span><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fiss&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckiana.a.raines%40nasa.gov%7C4f8d5ffaaefc458e396c08da9bdab7e6%7C7005d45845be48ae8140d43da96dd17b%7C0%7C0%7C637993660939626940%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=tORQzcWS9eXQrG0Y0nXeXlTWgq6nxoPDODMNaHH29aI%3D&amp;reserved=0"><span data-contrast="none">ISS Instagram</span></a><span data-contrast="none"> accounts.</span></p>
